ந்தை","parts":[{"text":"தந்தை","lemma":"tantai","gloss":"father"}],"gloss":"of the father"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெரிய","parts":[{"text":"பெரிய","lemma":"periya","gloss":"abundant/great"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"நறவின்","parts":[{"text":"நறவு","lemma":"naṟavu","gloss":"toddy/honey"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of toddy"},{"surface":"கூர்","parts":[{"text":"கூர்","lemma":"kūr","gloss":"sharp"}],"gloss":"sharp"},{"surface":"வேற்","parts":[{"text":"வேற்","lemma":"வேற்","gloss":"speared"}],"gloss":"speared","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பாரியது","parts":[{"text":"பாரி","lemma":"pāri","gloss":"Pāri"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of Pāri"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருமை","parts":[{"text":"அருமை","lemma":"arumai","gloss":"difficulty/greatness"}],"gloss":"difficulty"},{"surface":"அறியார்","parts":[{"text":"அறியார்","lemma":"aṟiyār","gloss":"not knowing (they)"}],"gloss":"not knowing"},{"surface":"போர்","parts":[{"text":"போர்","lemma":"pōr","gloss":"battle/war"}],"gloss":"battle"},{"surface":"எதிர்ந்து","parts":[{"text":"எதிர்ந்து","lemma":"etiṟntu","gloss":"having confronted"}],"gloss":"having confronted"},{"surface":"வந்த","parts":[{"text":"வந்த","lemma":"vanta","gloss":"who came"}],"gloss":"who came"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வலம்","parts":[{"text":"வலம்","lemma":"valam","gloss":"victory/strength"}],"gloss":"victorious"},{"surface":"படுதானை","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"possessing"},{"text":"தானை","lemma":"tāṉai","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"possessing army"},{"surface":"வேந்தர்","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தர்","lemma":"vēntar","gloss":"kings"}],"gloss":"kings"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொலம்","parts":[{"text":"பொலம்","lemma":"polam","gloss":"gold"}],"gloss":"gold"},{"surface":"படைக்","parts":[{"text":"படைக்","lemma":"படைக்","gloss":"ornamented"}],"gloss":"ornamented","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கலிமா","parts":[{"text":"கலி","lemma":"kali","gloss":"proud/spirited"},{"text":"மா","lemma":"mā","gloss":"horse"}],"gloss":"proud horses"},{"surface":"எண்ணு","parts":[{"text":"எண்ணு","lemma":"eṇṇu","gloss":"count"}],"gloss":"counting"},{"surface":"வோரே","parts":[{"text":"வோர்","lemma":"vōr","gloss":"those who"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"those who indeed"}]}],"literal":"Sweet water's great deep mountain pool blossomed blue water-lily's / opening buds' full-petalled wreaths rolling on the loins / of prominent beauty, cool rain-like eyes, and sweet smiles, women / in the lowly covered forked paths, thorny woven fenced / cotton front yard small houses there / sponge gourd sprouted bottle gourd climbing on the side / wild date-palm leaves' heap having climbed, salt merchants / salt weary cart caravan count, alas! / I grieve, I indeed! Let waste away my mornings! / On the dense dark mountain slope male monkeys having leaped and frolicking / even the male monkeys cannot consume so as to be, many also / even out of season trees fruit offering / fresh wealth unceasing vast mountain was like that indeed! / The lordly tall mountain peak having climbed, of the father / of abundant toddy and sharp speared Pāri / difficulty not knowing, battle having confronted who came / victorious possessing army kings / gold ornamented proud horses counting indeed!","translation":"The women with sweet smiles, cool rain-like eyes, and prominent beauty once wore full wreaths of opening blue water-lilies that bloomed in the deep, sweet-water mountain pools, rolling over their loins. Now, in small houses with cotton-drying front yards, fenced with thorny bushes along dusty, overgrown paths where sponge-gourds and bottle-gourds climb, salt-merchants climb onto heaps of wild-date leaves and count their weary salt-laden carts. Alas, I grieve! Let my mornings fade away! Once, on the dense, dark slopes of this vast mountain, male monkeys leaped and frolicked, and even when they could not consume it all, many trees yielded fruit out of season, offering unceasing fresh wealth. Such was the mountain of Pāri, who possessed abundant toddy and sharp spears. The kings with victorious armies who came to wage war, not knowing how difficult it was to conquer, once climbed his father's majestic tall peaks and proudly counted their gold-ornamented horses. Now, it is reduced to a place where salt-merchants count their carts.","modern":"இனிமையான நீர் கொண்ட பெரிய ஆழமான சுனைகளில் மலர்ந்த குவளை மலர்களின் இதழ்கள் அவிழ்ந்த மாலைகள் புரளும் அல்குலை உடைய, சிறந்த அழகும், குளிர்ச்சியான கண்களும், இனிய புன்னகையும் கொண்ட மகளிர் வாழ்ந்த இடம் அது. இப்போது, புழுதி நிறைந்த கவர்த்த வழிகளில், முள் வேலி அடைத்த, பருத்தி காயப்போடும் முற்றத்தைக் கொண்ட சிறிய வீடுகளின் அருகே, பீர்க்கங்கொடியும் சுரைக்கொடியும் படர்ந்திருக்கும் பகுதியில், ஈச்ச இலைகளின் குவியலின் மேல் ஏறி நின்று உமணர்கள் தங்களது உப்பு பாரம் ஏற்றிய வண்டிகளை எண்ணுகிறார்கள். ஐயோ, நான் வருந்துகிறேன்! என் வாழ்நாளின் காலைப் பொழுதுகள் அழிந்துபோகட்டும்! அடர்ந்த கரிய மலைச்சரிவுகளில் ஆண் குரங்குகள் பாய்ந்து விளையாடவும், அக்குரங்குகளாலும் தின்று தீர்க்க முடியாத அளவுக்குப் பல மரங்களும் காலம் அல்லாத காலத்திலும் பழங்களைத் தந்து, புதிய வளம் நீங்காத பரந்த மலையாக அது விளங்கியது. அத்தகைய சிறப்பு வாய்ந்த, தந்தை வழி வந்த உயர்ந்த மலை உச்சிக்கு ஏறி, மிகுந்த கள்ளையும் கூர்மையான வேலையும் உடைய பாரியின் அருமையை அறியாமல், அவனோடு போர் செய்ய வந்த வெற்றி பொருந்திய சேனைகளைக் கொண்ட மூவேந்தர்கள், பொன்னால் அலங்கரிக்கப்பட்ட தங்களது குதிரைகளை அன்று பெருமையோடு எண்ணிப் பார்த்தார்கள். இன்று அங்கே உமணர்கள் வண்டிகளை எண்ணுகிறார்கள்.","explanation":"This poem is a poignant lament (kaiyaṟunilai) by the poet Kapilar on the tragic fall of his beloved patron, King Vēḷ Pāri, and the desolation of his famous Parampu hill. Kapilar contrasts the glorious past of the mountain with its current ruined state after Pāri's death. In the past, the mountain was so fertile that trees yielded fruit out of season, and the kings of the three great Tamil dynasties who came to besiege it could only stand on the high peaks and count their vast cavalry, unable to conquer it. Now, the mountain is deserted, and instead of proud kings counting their gold-ornamented warhorses, poor salt-merchants climb on heaps of wild-date leaves to count their weary salt carts. The beautiful women who once wore fresh water-lilies from deep mountain pools are gone, replaced by desolate huts overgrown with wild gourds. This stark contrast between the past glory of Pāri's court and the present emptiness beautifully captures the deep grief of the poet.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,1.6],[1.6,2.22],[2.22,2.98],[2.98,3.6],[3.6,4.1],[4.1,4.5],[4.5,5.5],[5.5,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,6.4],[6.4,6.8],[7.1,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.1,8.6],[8.6,8.8],[8.8,9.0],[9.0,9.3],[9.3,10.3],[10.3,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.4],[11.4,12.4],[12.4,12.7],[12.7,12.9],[12.9,13.5],[13.5,14.0],[14.0,14.8],[14.8,15.2],[15.2,15.53],[15.53,16.2],[16.2,16.7],[16.7,16.9],[16.9,17.17],[17.17,17.53],[17.53,17.9],[18.68,19.28],[19.28,19.48],[19.48,20.38],[20.38,20.78],[20.78,21.68],[21.68,22.08],[22.08,22.48],[22.48,22.78],[22.78,23.14],[23.14,23.58],[23.58,24.48],[24.48,24.84],[24.84,25.2],[25.2,25.78],[25.78,26.78],[26.78,26.98],[26.98,27.18],[27.18,27.48],[27.48,27.88],[27.88,28.4],[28.4,28.83],[28.83,29.53],[29.53,29.96],[30.48,31.38],[31.38,31.78],[31.78,32.31],[32.31,32.85],[32.85,33.38],[33.38,33.58],[33.58,33.88],[33.88,34.28],[34.28,34.48],[34.48,35.05],[35.05,35.8],[35.8,36.18],[36.18,36.48],[36.48,36.88],[37.84,38.34],[38.34,38.64],[38.64,39.24],[39.24,39.54],[39.54,39.84],[39.84,40.14],[40.14,40.34],[40.34,40.74]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,2.32],[2.32,2.98],[2.98,3.5],[3.5,4.6],[4.6,5.0],[5.0,6.1],[6.1,6.4],[6.4,6.6],[6.6,6.9],[6.9,7.28],[7.28,8.03],[8.03,8.4],[8.4,8.9],[8.9,9.3],[9.3,9.5],[9.5,9.8],[9.8,10.1],[10.1,10.66],[10.66,11.4],[11.4,11.8],[11.8,12.3],[12.3,13.5],[13.5,13.8],[13.8,14.1],[14.1,14.7],[14.7,15.3],[15.3,15.9],[15.9,16.2],[16.2,16.62],[16.62,17.47],[17.47,18.1],[18.1,18.3],[18.3,18.5],[18.5,19.17],[19.3,19.7],[20.44,21.04],[21.04,21.24],[21.38,21.94],[21.94,22.34],[22.34,23.04],[23.04,23.34],[23.34,23.84],[23.84,24.04],[24.04,24.59],[24.59,25.29],[25.29,25.84],[25.84,26.2],[26.2,26.56],[26.56,27.04],[27.04,28.04],[28.04,28.24],[28.24,28.44],[28.44,28.74],[28.74,29.14],[29.14,29.72],[29.72,30.19],[30.19,30.99],[30.99,31.46],[32.04,32.84],[32.84,33.24],[33.24,33.59],[33.59,33.94],[33.94,35.04],[35.04,35.24],[35.24,35.64],[35.64,36.04],[36.04,36.24],[36.24,36.77],[36.77,37.48],[37.48,37.84],[37.84,38.14],[38.14,38.54],[39.6,40.3],[40.3,40.5],[40.5,41.3],[41.3,42.0],[42.0,42.3],[42.3,42.7],[42.7,42.9],[42.9,43.4]]},"sync":[[["தீநீர்ப்","of sweet water"]],[["பெருங்","great"]],[["குண்டு","deep"]],[["சுனைப்","mountain pool"]],[["பூத்த","blossomed"]],[["குவளைக்","blue water-lily"]],[["கூம்பவிழ்","opening buds"]],[["முழுநெறி","full-petalled wreaths"]],[["புரள்வரும்","rolling/swaying"]],[["அல்குல்","loins"]],[["ஏந்தெழில்","prominent beauty"]],[["மழைக்","cool rain-like"]],[["கண்","eyes"]],[["இன்","sweet"]],[["நகை","smile"]],[["மகளிர்","women"]],[["புன்","lowly"]],[["மூசு","covered"]],[["கவலைய","forked paths"]],[["முள்","thorny"]],[["முடை","woven"]],[["வேலிப்","fence"]],[["பஞ்சி","cotton"]],[["முன்றில்","front yard"]],[["சிற்றில்","small house"]],[["ஆங்கண்","in that place"]],[["பீரை","sponge gourd"]],[["நாறிய","sprouted"]],[["சுரை","bottle gourd"]],[["இவர்","climbing"]],[["மருங்கின்","on the side"]],[["ஈத்திலைக்","wild date-palm leaves"]],[["குப்பை","heap"]],[["ஏறி","having climbed"]],[["உமணர்","salt merchants"]],[["உப்பு","salt"]],[["ஓய்","weary"]],[["ஒழுகை","cart caravan"]],[["எண்ணுப","they count"]],[["மாதோ","alas!"]],[["நோகோ","I grieve"]],[["யானே","I indeed"]],[["தேய்கமா","let it waste away"]],[["காலை","my mornings"]],[["பயில்","dense"]],[["இருஞ்","dark"]],[["சிலம்பிற்","on the mountain slope"]],[["கலை","male monkey"]],[["பாய்ந்து","having leaped"]],[["உகளவும்","and frolicking"]],[["கலையுங்","even the male monkeys"]],[["கொள்ளா","cannot 